       }
      ],
      "xlabel": "x (radians)"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Solve $2\\cos^2x+\\sin x-1=0$ for $0\\degree\\leq x\\leq360\\degree$.",
     "steps": [
      "Replace $\\cos^2x=1-\\sin^2x$: $2-2\\sin^2x+\\sin x-1=0$, i.e. $2s^2-s-1=0$ with $s=\\sin x$.",
      "$(2s+1)(s-1)=0$: $s=-\\frac{1}{2}$ or $s=1$.",
      "$s=1$: $x=90\\degree$. $s=-\\frac{1}{2}$: $x=210\\degree$ or $330\\degree$."
     ],
     "answer": "$x=90\\degree,210\\degree,330\\degree$"
    }
   ],
